course: dictionary
lesson: 10914
title: Vocational: skills for work
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Vocational is a long word, but it has a clue: it is about work. A vocational course teaches practical skills for a job or trade, such as plumbing, cooking, hairdressing or car repair. «Vocational courses» help you learn how to do a job, not just learn facts about it.
explain: When you meet vocational, read the words around it. «Vocational training» and «vocational school» both sound like places where you learn to do something with your hands and your skills. If the words nearby mention a job, the word is probably about work. Try swapping in "job skills" to check that it still makes sense.
explain: Sometimes a name can sound kind and still hide something terrible. The sentences show this: «"Vocational training centre" has been used as a name for an internment camp, a camp where people are locked up without a fair trial.» The name does not tell the whole truth, so you need the clues around it to understand what a place really is.
fact: Vocational means to do with the skills needed for a particular job or trade.
fact: «Vocational courses» teach practical job skills like plumbing, cooking, hairdressing or car repair.
fact: A trade is a job that uses special skills, often with your hands, such as plumbing or carpentry.
fact: A good check is to swap in "job skills" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Some words hide terrible things: governments have called prison camps «vocational training centres». A name can sound harmless while the facts around it show something very different.
exercise: Which of these is a vocational course? | Reading poems for fun | Drawing pictures of the sea | Learning the names of old kings | *Learning plumbing to fix pipes
exercise: «Vocational training» teaches practical skills, so what is it aimed at? | *Getting ready for a job | Playing games outdoors | Helping you sleep better at night | Learning only about the stars
exercise: «"Vocational training centre" has been used as a name for an internment camp.» What does this show? | Words never change their meaning | *A name can sound kind but hide something terrible | Vocational always means a fun holiday | Camps are always named by children
test: What does vocational mean? | To do with sleeping and dreaming | To do with reading old books | To do with the weather and the seasons | *To do with the skills needed for a job or trade
test: Which subjects would a vocational school teach? | Sleeping and resting | Ancient history and maths only | Painting for fun in the park | *Cooking and hairdressing
exam: Mia says a vocational course is just a hobby club. Is she right? | *No, it teaches practical skills for a job | No, it teaches you to fly a plane for fun | Yes, it is only for playing games | Yes, because hobbies and jobs are the same
